# Count-only mode with 64 top-level perfect extensions: upstream computes
# C(n,k) as c*(n-k+1)/k in size_t, which overflows for n >= 63 (report.md
# B5). Go counts every C(n,k) exactly (63 items: 2^63 sets including the
# empty set) and saturates at 2^64-1 (64 items: 2^64 sets in total; 70
# items: C(70,28..42) and the total).
# deviation: report-B5
